  <head>
    <ce:title>Thermoelectric transport properties, Seebeck coefficient, and figure of merit ZT in doped bismuth telluride and lead chalcogenides</ce:title>
    <ce:abstract>
      <ce:simple-para>Direct thermal-to-electrical energy conversion depends on maximizing the dimensionless thermoelectric figure of merit ZT = S^2 sigma T / kappa. This paper examines the compositional variation and transport properties across Bi2Te3 and PbTe-based semiconductors.</ce:simple-para>
    </ce:abstract>
  </head>
  <body>
